(E) A plane wave along x, exp(i k x), on the linearized lattice Boltzmann map
    L(k) = diag(exp(-i k c_ix)) (I + A), reduced to the conserved modes to O(k^2):
    M = P + k P L1 P + k^2 [P L2 P + P L1 Q (I - L0)^-1 Q L1 P], L1 = -i C (I + A),
    L2 = -(1/2) C^2 (I + A), C = diag(c_ix). Coordinates a = delta rho, b = delta j_x:
      a' = a - i k b + k^2 m_aa a;   b' = b - i k c_s^2 a + k^2 m_bb b  (m_ab = m_ba = 0),
    the modes ln lambda = -+ i c_s k - Gamma k^2 with Gamma = -(m_aa + m_bb) / 2 - c_s^2 / 2,
    the longitudinal viscosity nu_L = 2 Gamma (25.5). The transverse modes (b_y, b_z)
    have lambda = 1 exactly: no shear viscosity.
