(I) The lamp's content under its own release: the turn accumulator gains M(t) x n
    per self-creation and pays h b s_t, s_t its whole part in units of d (engine.py
    `_frame_all`, by_drive). The Bell lamp (examples/events/bell): M_0 = K + 2,
    K = 2^20 = [1, K], h = 1, b = 2 directions; registered: one stall, at tick 4,
    159 births in 160.
  the recurrence: births 159, stalls at ticks [4], content after 160 ticks 1048260
  |M(t) - M_0 (1 - r)^t| over the run at most 1.999992 < h b = 2 (25.9's bound)
